## 10. Code-mutation discipline

The specification suite was audited against mutation avoidance principles (`02-spec/02-coding-guidelines/01-cross-language/18-code-mutation-avoidance.md`):

- **Zustand Store Updates:** State mutations in `05-frontend-ui-and-state-management.md` use immutable object spreading (`set(state => ({ ...state, accounts: [...state.accounts, newAccount] }))`).
- **Database Schema Migrations:** DDL updates specified in `04-modules-storage-and-persistence.md` and `02-spec/23-app-db/01-index.md` are additive (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS`).
- **Log Buffering:** Proxy request logging inserts immutable records without in-place mutation of existing history rows.
- **Defect:** Lack of an explicit section citing `18-code-mutation-avoidance.md` in `05-frontend-ui` or `01-index.md`.
- **Score:** **92 / 100**.

